---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Showrunner — Make your pull request worth watching" description="Ask your agent to turn an application change into a verified, replayable Playwright demo with Showrunner." active="home"><main id="main">
			<section class="wrap hero">
				<p class="eyebrow">
					<span class="signal" aria-hidden="true"></span> THE CHANGE IS THE STORY
				</p>
				<h1>Make your pull request<br /><em>worth watching.</em></h1>
				<p class="intro">
					Ask your agent to demo the change.<br class="desktop-break" />
					It writes the scenario, checks the outcome, and records the story.
				</p>
				<div class="actions">
					<a class="button primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Get the agent skill</a
					><a class="text-link" href="#demo">See the sequence</a>
				</div>
				<p class="hero-note">
					<img class="brand-icon" src="/assets/playwright.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20" />An
					agent skill. A Playwright library. A repeatable first take.
				</p>
			</section>
			<section class="wrap demo-section" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
				<div class="section-label">
					<h2 id="demo-title">A small change. A clear story.</h2>
					<span>INTERACTIVE ILLUSTRATION / 4 STEPS</span>
				</div>
				<div class="stage">
					<div class="stage-top">
						<span><span class="record-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> FIRST TAKE</span
						><span>release-checklist.demo.ts</span
						><span class="stage-format">PLAYWRIGHT + SHOWRUNNER</span>
					</div>
					<div class="scene">
						<div class="scene-context">
							<span class="eyebrow">THE SCENE</span>
							<p>A release checklist.<br />One task to ship.</p>
							<span class="take-label">TAKE 001</span>
						</div>
						<div class="app-window">
							<div class="window-bar">
								<span aria-hidden="true">● ● ●</span><span>your-app / release</span>
							</div>
							<div class="app-content">
								<p class="app-label">WORKSPACE / RELEASE</p>
								<h3>Ready for the next release.</h3>
								<p>Good work deserves a good handoff.</p>
								<div class="mock-field">
									<span>Task</span>
									<div>
										<span id="demo-input">Draft task</span
										><span class="mock-add">Add task <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div class="checklist-item" id="demo-result">
									<span class="empty-mark" aria-hidden="true">○</span> Your next task starts here.
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="caption" id="demo-caption">01 / Set the scene with a chapter card.</div>
					</div>
					<div class="stage-bottom">
						<div class="sequence" aria-label="Demo sequence">
							<span class="active" data-step="0">01 <span>Set the scene</span></span
							><span data-step="1">02 <span>Type</span></span
							><span data-step="2">03 <span>Act</span></span
							><span data-step="3">04 <span>Assert</span></span>
						</div>
						<button class="next-step" id="demo-next" hidden>
							Next step <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
						</button>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="demo-footnote">
					An illustration of the workflow, not a recorded run.
					<a href="/docs/getting-started/#first">Run the real, self-contained demo</a>
				</p>
				<p class="sr-only" id="demo-status" role="status"></p>
			</section>
			<section class="wrap workflow" id="workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
				<div class="section-intro">
					<p class="eyebrow">LESS “HERE’S WHAT I CHANGED.”</p>
					<h2 id="workflow-title">More “here’s<br />how it works.”</h2>
					<p>A diff explains the implementation. A demo shows what the change feels like to use.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="steps">
					<article>
						<span class="step-number">01</span>
						<div>
							<h3>Point your agent at the change.</h3>
							<p>
								The skill guides your agent through the diff and your app’s existing routes,
								authentication, fixtures, and data.
							</p>
						</div>
					</article>
					<article>
						<span class="step-number">02</span>
						<div>
							<h3>Let it write and verify the story.</h3>
							<p>
								Your agent writes a Playwright scenario with meaningful assertions, then runs it
								without presentation delays to check the outcome.
							</p>
						</div>
					</article>
					<article>
						<span class="step-number">03</span>
						<div>
							<h3>Get a recording you can replay.</h3>
							<p>
								The agent records with readable pacing and reports the video, trace, and any
								limitations. The scenario stays with your app for the next change.
							</p>
						</div>
					</article>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section class="code-section" id="example">
				<div class="wrap code-layout">
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">STANDARD LOCATORS. BETTER PRESENTATION.</p>
						<h2>A little direction.<br />Still your test.</h2>
						<p>
							Presentation delays set the pace. Playwright’s actionability checks and your
							assertions establish that the app is ready.
						</p>
						<a
							class="light-link"
							href="/docs/api/"
							>Explore the presentation API</a
						>
						<p class="code-note">
							Set <code>pace: 0</code> for verification.<br />Keep the pacing for the recording.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="code-window">
						<div class="code-title"><span>profile.demo.ts</span><span>TYPESCRIPT</span></div>
						<pre is:raw
							tabindex="0"
							aria-label="Example Showrunner scenario"
						><code><span class="code-purple">import</span> { test, expect } <span class="code-purple">from</span> <span class="code-green">"@smeltery/showrunner"</span>;

test(<span class="code-green">"save a display name"</span>, <span class="code-purple">async</span> ({ page, demo }) =&gt; {
  <span class="code-purple">await</span> page.goto(<span class="code-green">"/settings/profile"</span>);
  <span class="code-purple">await</span> demo.caption(<span class="code-green">"Make it yours."</span>);
  <span class="code-purple">await</span> demo.fill(
    page.getByRole(<span class="code-green">"textbox"</span>, { name: <span class="code-green">"Display name"</span> }),
    <span class="code-green">"River"</span>
  );
  <span class="code-purple">await</span> demo.click(page.getByRole(<span class="code-green">"button"</span>, { name: <span class="code-green">"Save"</span> }));
  <span class="code-purple">await</span> expect(page.getByRole(<span class="code-green">"status"</span>))
    .toHaveText(<span class="code-green">"Profile saved"</span>);
});</code></pre>
						<p>Adapt the route and accessible names to your application.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section class="wrap closing">
				<p class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT PR HAS A STORY.</p>
				<h2>Give it a good first take.</h2>
				<p>
					Give your agent the skill and a change to demonstrate. Keep the scenario with your code.
				</p>
				<a class="button primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Set up the agent skill</a>
				<p class="availability">Public package on GitHub Packages · Release downloads and local builds</p>
			</section>
		</main></Base>
